  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "After glycolysis and the citric acid cycle, most of the energy that came out of the glucose is carried by two molecules: N A D H and F A D H two."
   ],
   [
    11.081,
    "They are loaded with electrons, and they donate them to the electron transport chain."
   ],
   [
    15.977,
    "The chain sits in the inner membrane of the mitochondrion, the membrane folded into cristae."
   ],
   [
    21.836,
    "Those folds give the membrane much more surface, so there is room for a great many chains."
   ],
   [
    27.422,
    "Most of the parts of the chain are proteins, grouped into multiprotein complexes."
   ],
   [
    33.086,
    "We number them one, two, three and four."
   ]
  ]
